  "details": "I use GTAvaCrypt for shader encryption. This uses 32 bool parameters as key, as you can see in image #1. This 32 bools has to be synced completely, so the other players will see an fully decrypted avatar.\nNon beta/ik-beta (1194.9): As you can see on image #2, all looks normal. On left side, it's my view with an encrypted Merino (tall). On the right side, it's a friends view (Mini-Mint). All looks good when Mint looks at Merino. Merino is fully decrypted for both.\nOpen beta (1197): On the image #3, the result looks good on the left side view for me. But on the right friends side, the mesh on Merino looks broken (decryption partially fails).\nIn the image #4, custom animations are disabled on the right friends view. This is, how it looks, when nothing will be decrypted (looks like expected). \nConclusion:\nI don't know, whats exactly wrong. But it seems, like the most bools will be synced, but not all (because of the difference between image #3 and #4). Maybe there is a bug for bool syncing?\nBTW: I use the latest SDK (VRCSDK3-AVATAR-2022.05.12.23.07_Public).",
